WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.743
Marks.

2
00:00:00.903 --> 00:00:02.436
Art starts with a mark.

3
00:00:02.596 --> 00:00:06.961
A mark is anything you leave on the paper: a dot, a dab, a line.

4
00:00:07.121 --> 00:00:09.164
A pencil makes one kind of mark.

5
00:00:09.324 --> 00:00:10.764
A brush makes another.

6
00:00:10.924 --> 00:00:12.364
A sponge makes another.

7
00:00:12.524 --> 00:00:14.056
Your finger makes one too.

8
00:00:14.756 --> 00:00:15.963
Kinds of line.

9
00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:19.374
A line is a mark that goes from one place to another.

10
00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.485
It can be straight, like a ruler.

11
00:00:21.645 --> 00:00:23.038
Wavy, like the sea.

12
00:00:23.198 --> 00:00:24.870
Zigzag, like lightning.

13
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.516
Dotted, like footprints.

14
00:00:26.676 --> 00:00:28.905
Thick, like a trunk, or thin, like a thread.

15
00:00:29.605 --> 00:00:30.905
Try every tool.

16
00:00:31.065 --> 00:00:33.434
Artists try every tool to see what it does.

17
00:00:33.594 --> 00:00:36.473
A brush cannot make a thin line as well as a pencil.

18
00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:39.698
A pencil cannot make a big soft dab like a sponge.

19
00:00:39.858 --> 00:00:42.412
Knowing what each tool does is how you choose.

20
00:00:43.112 --> 00:00:44.645
Lines from long ago.

21
00:00:44.805 --> 00:00:52.653
Thousands of years ago, people drew animals on cave walls with thick dark lines, and pressed their hands on the wall to leave a mark.

22
00:00:52.813 --> 00:00:54.346
Their marks are still there.

23
00:00:54.506 --> 00:00:55.806
Yours can be too.
